20. Also calls on the international community to continue to support the National Human  Rights  Commission,  through  technical  assistance  and  capacity-building programmes,  with  a  view  to  enabling  it  to  contribute  effectively  to  the  promotion  and protection  of  the  fundamental  rights  of  the  Ivorian  people,  in  accordance  with  the  Paris Principles;
21. Decides therefore  to  extend  the  mandate  on  capacity-building  and  technical cooperation with Côte d’Ivoire in the field of human rights for a period of one year, from the twenty-ninth to the thirty-second sessions of the Human Rights Council;
22. Requests the  Independent  Expert  to  submit  a  report  to  the  Human  Rights Council at its thirty-first session and his final recommendations at its thirty-second session;
23. Decides to remain seized of this matter.

